# Example 8: Epigenetic regulation - DNA methylation + histone modification
# Concept demo: effects of epigenetic modifications on gene expression
#
# This .helix file declares epigenetic modifications via the #methylate and #histone bio-instruction annotations,
# targeting regulated_gene; the Python API comments below supplement with equivalent script calls.
#
# Data sources:
# - Dam methylation: GATC sites (Marinus 1973)
# - CpG methylation: CG sites (Bird 2002)
# - H3K4me3: active promoter (+0.5)
# - H3K27me3: Polycomb repression (-0.7)
# - DNA methylation represses gene expression by ~70% (Bird 2002)

#promoter name=p_epigenetic strength=0.5
#gene name=regulated_gene promoter=p_epigenetic
ATG GCT GCT GCT GCT GCT GCT TAA
#end

# Regulation: epigenetic modifications indirectly affect expression via expression-modifier factors
#regulate p_epigenetic -> regulated_gene strength=+0.8

# Epigenetic instructions: apply Dam methylation + H3K4me3 histone marks to regulated_gene
# The parser records them as two BioInstructions (kind=methylate / histone, target=regulated_gene)
#methylate target=regulated_gene methylase=dam level=0.8
#histone target=regulated_gene mark=H3K4me3 level=0.9

